      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Antonia purchased a bag of rice and some carrots at the grocery store. Antonia paid \\$2 for the bag\nof rice and \\$1.70 per pound for the carrots. If Antonia paid a total of \\$10.50 for the bag of rice\nand the carrots, which of the following equations can be used to find $p$, the number of pounds of\ncarrots Antonia purchased? (Assume there is no sales tax.)"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-25e21d56d2d24b16b70a16a8dc1d21c3",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q1"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.70 p+2=10.50$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.70 p - 2=10.50$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.70+2 p=10.50$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$1.70 - 2 p=10.50$$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
